---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What is the Animus Project?",
    answer: "Animus is an open initiative to map the collective mind and opinions of humanity in real time. We capture authentic human perspectives without algorithms or noise, organizing them into a living, interconnected graph database."
  },
  {
    question: "Is the application free to use?",
    answer: "Yes, 100% free for everyone. There are no fees or paywalls to answer questions, participate in community topics, or explore real-time demographic consensus."
  },
  {
    question: "Why must I answer a question before seeing the results?",
    answer: "To eliminate psychological herd bias. In traditional feeds or polls, seeing existing votes beforehand inevitably skews your answer. In Animus, committing your authentic stance first unlocks the raw, uninfluenced truth."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the reciprocity and credit system work?",
    answer: "Animus operates on 'Give to Ask'. Answering community questions earns you participation credits. Those credits give you the right to post your own questions and boost them to reach broader local and global feeds."
  },
  {
    question: "What personal information does Animus collect?",
    answer: "We deliberately do not want your personal identity. No real names, no phone books, and no surveillance tracking. We only request non-identifiable demographic markers (age bracket, gender, and general region) to reveal societal patterns."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the graph database handle duplicate questions?",
    answer: "When multiple people ask identical or closely related questions, Animus intelligently merges them into a single knowledge node. This concentrates volume, eliminates fragmentation, and builds deep statistical clarity."
  },
  {
    question: "Who benefits from this data?",
    answer: "Humanity. Sociologists, behavioral scientists, educators, and the general public gain access to an authentic mirror of what people actually think and worry about, rather than what ad-driven algorithms amplify."
  }
];
---

<section id="faq" class="py-28 bg-white dark:bg-[#09090b] relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-3xl relative z-10">
    <div class="text-center mb-16 reveal-on-scroll">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-primary-300 dark:border-primary-500/30 bg-primary-50 dark:bg-primary-500/10 text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">
        FAQ
      </span>
      <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-sans font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
        Everything you need to know about the Animus Project.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4">
      {faqs.map((faq, index) => (
        <details class="group glass-panel rounded-2xl [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden reveal-on-scroll" style={`transition-delay: ${index * 50}ms;`}>
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-1.5 p-6 text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-medium">
            <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-sans font-bold">{faq.question}</h3>
            <span class="relative h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 group-open:text-primary-600 dark:group-open:text-primary-400 transition-colors">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="absolute inset-0 h-5 w-5 opacity-100 group-open:opacity-0 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" />
              </svg>
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="absolute inset-0 h-5 w-5 opacity-0 group-open:opacity-100 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M20 12H4" />
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-sans text-sm sm:text-base">
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
